  "name": "Bambu Lab H2S (0.8 mm nozzle; stock quick-swap hotend and ducts)",
  "provenance": "H2S single-nozzle H2 toolhead. Nozzle: tip bands of the Bambu quick-swap hotend (0.6 mm land, 35-degree cone capped at 2 mm radius, from https://www.printables.com/model/533213 Hotend.STEP as in bambu-a1), clipped at the BambuStudio nozzle_height floor; Bambu's FAQ says this nozzle family is shared by H2D and P2S (https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/p2s/manual/p2s-faq) and its High Flow hotend is sold for H2/P2S (https://us.store.bambulab.com/products/bambu-high-flow-hotend-h2-p2s). BambuStudio H2S preset (https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio/tree/master/resources/profiles/BBL/machine): nozzle_height 4 (common), extruder_clearance_height_to_rod 33, dist_to_rod 56, max_radius 81 -> gantry underside Z 33, symmetric Y span +-56, infinite X; head half-width 34 mm (81 mm print-by-object radius vs 65 on P1S at +-35). Ducts start at the 4 mm floor (outlets X +-8..24), outer walls to X +-34, risers from Z 9, cover Z 24. Toolhead photos: https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/h2/maintenance/replace-nozzle-lifting-rail . Body boxes are estimates from Bambu wiki/store toolhead photos with the BambuStudio clearances as hard anchors; axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Derived 2026-11-11; calibrated=false. Nozzle variant: 0.8 mm bore, 1.0 mm land, same cone and shoulder as bambu-a1-nozzle-08.",
